      "message": "There may be cases where there is a \"cellular\" network but telephony isn\u0027t declared using a transport override for ethernet. Therefore, we should not check the telephony data feature.\n\nIn this case, what you should really do is check if the current default network is a cellular and metered. The easiest way may be to use the synchronous method `getActiveNetwork` https://developer.android.com/reference/android/net/ConnectivityManager#getActiveNetwork(), then check if the returned network is cellular and metered. If so, you can then disable it.",
